  "@signInNoCodeHelp": {
    "description": "UNCONDITIONAL on the code step, in both locales. Not gated on the delivery stub and not gated on a failure: a code that does not arrive is the one situation where a diner has no way forward, and the lockout design assumes a human can be reached (see the decision doc). The contact itself is a PLACEHOLDER that FAILS THE BUILD until a real one is supplied — see support_contact.dart and support_contact_test.dart. The ADDRESS ITSELF is no longer interpolated here: it is a separate tappable widget, because making the whole sentence a link would give the link the sentence as its accessible name."
  },
  "@signInNameWhy": {
    "description": "The name step is reached only after a correct code, so the number is already proved. This sentence has to justify one more field to somebody who thought they had finished — hence 'nothing else is needed', which is also true."
  }
